 "validation": {
  "check_1_sum_price_equals_pot": "PASS - sum of the 32 entry prices = $21,145.00 = workbook pot ($21,145.00 at 'Calcutta Live Draft'!L24, the cell the Realized Return formula multiplies by). Delta $0.00. Prices also agree cell-for-cell between 'Calcutta Live Draft' Value Paid and Returns!E on all 32 lots (Returns!E is a direct link, ='Calcutta Live Draft'!D7 style).",
  "check_2_shares_sum_to_one": "PASS - all 32 entries sum to exactly 1.0. Calcutta III has NO split ownership: the Returns tab has a single Owner column with no slash strings and no 'Owner #2' column, and the '# Teams' column in the Players block is integer for every owner (4/2/3/7/12/4 = 32). Failures: none.",
  "check_3_points_denominator": "N/A-BY-DESIGN, reported as required. Calcutta III has no points column of any kind, so there is no points total and no points denominator. Its arithmetic is a pure percent-of-pot model: Returns!O = SUMPRODUCT(pct_row F1:N1, splits_row F2:N2, metric_row) * PotSize. I derived the implied denominator anyway by the requested method (metric-share x pot / payout) and it comes out to 1.000000000 (i.e. 100% of the pot), NOT 11,420. Summing the nine rule shares over all 32 teams gives 0.999999999998 of the pot (float noise on the 1/52 split), i.e. the rubric exhausts exactly 100% of the pot by construction: wins 272 x 0.10% = 27.20%; 20+ Pt Wins pool 5.00%; Weekly Big Winner 18 x 0.50% = 9.00%; Reg. Season BigWin 1 x 0.30% = 0.30%; Playoff Berth 14 x 0.75% = 10.50%; Div. Round 8 x 1.50% = 12.00%; Conf. Round 4 x 3.00% = 12.00%; SB Berth 2 x 6.00% = 12.00%; Win Super Bowl 1 x 12.00% = 12.00%. Total = 100.00%.",
  "check_4_payout_recompute": "PASS - recomputed all 32 payouts end to end from events + rules; largest absolute error $0.00000023 (float noise). Worked arithmetic, five teams: (a) Buffalo 11 wins x 0.10% + 5 20+pt-wins x (5.00%/52) + 2 weekly-big-winner x 0.50% + berth 0.75% + div 1.50% = 1.10% + 0.9615385% + 1.00% + 0.75% + 1.50% = 5.3115385% x $21,145 = $1,021.4662 vs workbook $1,021.466154. (b) Baltimore 13 x 0.10% + 4 x (5.00%/52) + 3 x 0.50% + 0.75% + 1.50% + 3.00% = 1.30% + 0.7692308% + 1.50% + 5.25% = 8.4342308% x $21,145 = $1,783.4994 vs $1,783.499423. (c) Kansas City 11 x 0.10% + 1 x (5.00%/52) + 0.75% + 1.50% + 3.00% + 6.00% + 12.00% = 1.10% + 0.0961538% + 23.25% = 24.4461538% x $21,145 = $5,169.1392 vs $5,169.139231. (d) Dallas 12 x 0.10% + 9 x (5.00%/52) + 5 x 0.50% + 0.75% = 1.20% + 0.8653846% + 2.50% + 0.75% = 5.3153846% x $21,145 = $1,123.9381 vs $1,123.938077. (e) San Francisco 12 x 0.10% + 4 x (5.00%/52) + 0.75% + 1.50% + 3.00% + 6.00% = 1.20% + 0.7692308% + 11.25% = 13.2192308% x $21,145 = $2,713.8794 vs $2,713.879423. All five match to the cent.",
  "check_5_owner_costs_and_returns": "PASS - rebuilding owner cost and realized return from entry-level data (all shares 1.0) reproduces the Players block exactly for all 6 owners: Anthony C. $2,180 / $3,281.541346; Craig T. $1,070 / $443.2317308; Ed Z. $2,425 / $1,296.351154; Sam R. $5,640 / $4,982.087308; Zach L. $5,455 / $4,898.320577; Zack M. $4,375 / $6,243.467885. Summing the 14 transcribed trade legs' Net Trade Value by the workbook's 'New Owner' column reproduces 'Impact of Trades' for all 6 (Anthony +186.076, Craig 0, Ed +182.6114731, Sam -1,171.048742, Zach +802.3612692, Zack 0) and the legs net to exactly $0.00 across the pool. cost/realized/trade_impact then rebuild 'Net Return' for all 6. Mismatches: none.",
  "check_6_pot_exhaustion": "PASS - sum of all 32 Realized Returns = $21,145.0000006 = pot to float noise, so the workbook divides by a fixed schedule of pot percentages that happens to add to exactly 100%; it does NOT renormalize to points earned. normalization = 'direct' is what the arithmetic shows.",
